1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,400
No signal in the basement.
The technician taps Done.

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:09,400
Many apps send that tap to the
server first. No signal, no save.

3
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:13,600
Offline-first apps save it in
phone storage first. No waiting.

4
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:17,300
Each visit also joins
a queue for the server.

5
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:21,900
Visits two and three, still in the
basement. Each saves instantly.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,150
The queue holds all
three. Nothing is lost.

7
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:29,150
Signal’s back. The queue sends
each visit to the server…

8
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:32,550
…in the order they happened.

9
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:35,950
Signal gone again. Now
save on the server first.

10
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:38,750
Same three taps. Nothing saved.

11
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:41,050
That spinner is a design choice.

12
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:45,000
Ask your team: where
does a tap save first?
